SimTime [SimTalk]
Returns the current simulation time of the EventController designated by <Path>.
Type
Read-only attribute
Syntax
<Path>.SimTime → time
Watchable
The read-only attribute is watchable.
Note
You can, for example, watch the SimTime value with an object of type Display or Chart. You should
never use SimTime in a method, which affects the simulation, with a waituntil-instruction or a
stopuntil-instruction.
The time does not advance continuously, but jumps from event to event. If you activate the animation,
Plant Simulation generates additional events so that the waituntil-instruction or stopuntil-instruction
might be woken up at an earlier point in time than intended.
Return Value
The return value has the data type time.
Examples
param sensorID: integer, Front: boolean
if @.ID = 1 
   @.Speed := 0
   print EventController.SimTime, " The first Transporter stopped."
end
print "Machine was deactivated at:",
root.EventController.SimTime."
See also
Time [EventController]
SimTime [SimTalk]
